2026-10-20T21:06:14.1615441Z             fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1616120Z +             text: 'Using user-controlled data to create a template can lead to remote code execution or cross site scripting.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1671657Z -             text: 'User input should not be used in regular expressions without first being escaped, otherwise a malicious user may be able to inject an expression that could require exponential time on certain inputs.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1671776Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1671869Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1672113Z +             markdown: '# Server Side Template Injection\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1673141Z +               'A template from a server templating engine such as Jinja constructed from user input can allow the user to execute arbitrary code using certain template features. It can also allow for cross-site scripting.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1673363Z -             markdown: '# Regular expression injection\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1675180Z -               'Constructing a regular expression with unsanitized user input is dangerous as a malicious user may be able to modify the meaning of the expression. In particular, such a user may be able to provide a regular expression fragment that takes exponential time in the worst case, and use that to perform a Denial of Service attack.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1675525Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1675619Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1675750Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1677015Z +               'Ensure that an untrusted value is not used to directly construct a template. Jinja also provides `SandboxedEnvironment` that prohibits access to unsafe methods and attributes. This can be used if constructing a template from user input is absolutely necessary.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1677963Z -               "Before embedding user input into a regular expression, use a sanitization function such as `re.escape` to escape meta-characters that have a special meaning regarding regular expressions' syntax.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1678047Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1678136Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1678263Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1678860Z +               'In the following case, `template` is used to generate a Jinja2 template string. This can lead to remote code execution.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1679238Z -               'The following examples are based on a simple Flask web server environment.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1679325Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1679954Z -               'The following example shows a HTTP request parameter that is used to construct a regular expression without sanitizing it first:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1680046Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1680177Z +               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1680359Z +               'from django.urls import path\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1680567Z +               'from django.http import HttpResponse\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1680757Z +               'from jinja2 import Template, escape\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1680848Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1680954Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1681133Z +               'def a(request):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1681344Z +               "    template = request.GET['template']\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1681450Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1681708Z +               '    # BAD: Template is constructed from user input. \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1681887Z +               '    t = Template(template)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1681981Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1682163Z +               "    name = request.GET['name']\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1682364Z +               '    html = t.render(name=escape(name))\n' +
