2026-10-20T21:06:14.1784441Z             fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1784979Z +             text: 'Building a XPath query from user-controlled sources is vulnerable to insertion of malicious Xpath code by the user.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1785406Z -             text: 'URL redirection based on unvalidated user input may cause redirection to malicious web sites.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1785487Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1785573Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1785837Z +             markdown: '# XPath query built from user-controlled sources\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1786676Z +               'If an XPath expression is built using string concatenation, and the components of the concatenation include user input, it makes it very easy for a user to create a malicious XPath expression.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1786895Z -             markdown: '# URL redirection from remote source\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1788212Z -               'Directly incorporating user input into a URL redirect request without validating the input can facilitate phishing attacks. In these attacks, unsuspecting users can be redirected to a malicious site that looks very similar to the real site they intend to visit, but which is controlled by the attacker.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1788299Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1788384Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1788508Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1789269Z +               'If user input must be included in an XPath expression, either sanitize the data or use variable references to safely embed it without altering the structure of the expression.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1790328Z -               'To guard against untrusted URL redirection, it is advisable to avoid putting user input directly into a redirect URL. Instead, maintain a list of authorized redirects on the server; then choose from that list based on the user input provided.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1790416Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1791340Z -               'If this is not possible, then the user input should be validated in some other way, for example, by verifying that the target URL does not include an explicit host name.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1791430Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1791528Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1791636Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1792080Z +               'In the example below, the xpath query is controlled by the user and hence leads to a vulnerability.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1792781Z -               'The following example shows an HTTP request parameter being used directly in a URL redirect without validating the input, which facilitates phishing attacks:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1792859Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1792942Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1793056Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1793202Z +               'from lxml import etree\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1793361Z +               'from io import StringIO\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1793566Z -               'from flask import Flask, request, redirect\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1793644Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1794016Z +               'from django.urls import path\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1794353Z +               'from django.http import HttpResponse\n' +
