2026-10-20T21:06:14.1923037Z -           fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1923454Z -             text: 'Cookies with `SameSite` set to `None` can allow for Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) attacks.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1923535Z -           },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1923633Z -           help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1924208Z -             markdown: '# Sensitive cookie with `SameSite` attribute set to `None`\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1925444Z -               "Cookies with the `SameSite` attribute set to `'None'` will be sent with cross-origin requests. This can sometimes allow for Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) attacks, in which a third-party site could perform actions on behalf of a user, if the cookie is used for authentication.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1925537Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1925619Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1925744Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1928327Z +               'If user input must be included in an LDAP query or DN, it should be escaped to avoid a malicious user providing special characters that change the meaning of the query. In Python2, user input should be escaped with `ldap.dn.escape_dn_chars` or `ldap.filter.escape_filter_chars`, while in Python3, user input should be escaped with `ldap3.utils.dn.escape_rdn` or `ldap3.utils.conv.escape_filter_chars` depending on the component tainted by the user. A good practice is to escape filter characters that could change the meaning of the query (https://tools.ietf.org/search/rfc4515\\#section-3).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1929221Z -               "Set the `samesite` to `Lax` or `Strict`, or add `; SameSite=Lax;`, or `; SameSite=Strict;` to the cookie's raw header value. The default value in most cases is `Lax`.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1929310Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1929396Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1929515Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1930084Z +               'In the following examples, the code accepts both `username` and `dc` from the user, which it then uses to build a LDAP query and DN.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1930689Z -               'In the following examples, the cases marked GOOD show secure cookie attributes being set; whereas in the case marked BAD they are not set.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1930777Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1931930Z +               'The first and the second example uses the unsanitized user input directly in the search filter and DN for the LDAP query. A malicious user could provide special characters to change the meaning of these components, and search for a completely different set of values.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1932019Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1932118Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1932225Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1932401Z +               'from flask import request, Flask\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1932655Z +               'import ldap\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1932918Z -               'from flask import Flask, request, make_response, Response\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1933003Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1933083Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1933238Z +               '@app.route("/normal")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1933371Z +               'def normal():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1933549Z +               "    unsafe_dc = request.args['dc']\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1933761Z +               "    unsafe_filter = request.args['username']\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1934162Z -               '@app.route("/good1")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1934296Z -               'def good1():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1934459Z -               '    resp = make_response()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1935019Z -               `    resp.set_cookie("sessionid", value="value", secure=True, httponly=True, samesite='Strict') # GOOD: Attributes are securely set\n` +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1935165Z -               '    return resp\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1935252Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1935425Z +               '    dn = "dc={}".format(unsafe_dc)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1935664Z +               '    search_filter = "(user={})".format(unsafe_filter)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1935750Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1936001Z +               '    ldap_connection = ldap.initialize("ldap://127.0.0.1")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1936191Z +               '    user = ldap_connection.search_s(\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1936400Z +               '        dn, ldap.SCOPE_SUBTREE, search_filter)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1936543Z -               '@app.route("/good2")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1936681Z -               'def good2():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1936837Z -               '    resp = make_response()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1937365Z -               `    resp.headers['Set-Cookie'] = "sessionid=value; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Strict" # GOOD: Attributes are securely set \n` +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1937506Z -               '    return resp\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1937585Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1937728Z -               '@app.route("/bad1")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1937854Z -               'def bad1():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1938009Z -               '    resp = make_response()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1938783Z -               `    resp.set_cookie("sessionid", value="value", samesite='None') # BAD: the SameSite attribute is set to 'None' and the 'Secure' and 'HttpOnly' attributes are set to False by default.\n` +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1938918Z -               '    return resp\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.1939002Z                 '```\n' +
