2026-10-20T21:06:14.2051109Z             fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2051809Z +             text: 'Interpreting unsanitized user input as code allows a malicious user to perform arbitrary code execution.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2052273Z -             text: 'Logging sensitive information without encryption or hashing can expose it to an attacker.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2052362Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2052451Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2052625Z +             markdown: '# Code injection\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2054264Z +               'Directly evaluating user input (for example, an HTTP request parameter) as code without properly sanitizing the input first allows an attacker arbitrary code execution. This can occur when user input is passed to code that interprets it as an expression to be evaluated, such as `eval` or `exec`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2054551Z -             markdown: '# Clear-text logging of sensitive information\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2055040Z -               'If sensitive data is written to a log entry it could be exposed to an attacker who gains access to the logs.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2055126Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2056147Z -               'Potential attackers can obtain sensitive user data when the log output is displayed. Additionally that data may expose system information such as full path names, system information, and sometimes usernames and passwords.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2056389Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2056530Z +               '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2057690Z +               'Avoid including user input in any expression that may be dynamically evaluated. If user input must be included, use context-specific escaping before including it. It is important that the correct escaping is used for the type of evaluation that will occur.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2057777Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2057866Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2057997Z +               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2059820Z +               'The following example shows two functions setting a name from a request. The first function uses `exec` to execute the `setname` function. This is dangerous as it can allow a malicious user to execute arbitrary code on the server. For example, the user could supply the value `"\' + subprocess.call(\'rm -rf\') + \'"` to destroy the server\'s file system. The second function calls the `setname` function directly and is thus safe.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2059918Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2060011Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2060133Z +               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2060224Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2060369Z +               'urlpatterns = [\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2060537Z +               '    # Route to code_execution\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2060840Z +               "    url(r'^code-ex1$', code_execution_bad, name='code-execution-bad'),\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2061141Z +               "    url(r'^code-ex2$', code_execution_good, name='code-execution-good')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2061236Z +               ']\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2061330Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2061496Z +               'def code_execution(request):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2061673Z +               "    if request.method == 'POST':\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2062009Z +               "        first_name = base64.decodestring(request.POST.get('first_name', ''))\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2062235Z +               '        #BAD -- Allow user to define code to be run.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2062427Z +               `        exec("setname('%s')" % first_name)\n` +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2062521Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2062686Z +               'def code_execution(request):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2062852Z +               "    if request.method == 'POST':\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2063177Z +               "        first_name = base64.decodestring(request.POST.get('first_name', ''))\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2063355Z +               '        #GOOD --Call code directly\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2063643Z +               '        setname(first_name)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2063744Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2064055Z +               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2064168Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2064307Z +               '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2064642Z +               '* OWASP: [Code Injection](https://www.owasp.org/index.php/Code_Injection).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2064987Z +               '* Wikipedia: [Code Injection](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Code_injection).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2065391Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-94](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2065777Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-95](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/95.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2066179Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-116](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/116.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2066332Z +             text: '# Code injection\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2067630Z +               'Directly evaluating user input (for example, an HTTP request parameter) as code without properly sanitizing the input first allows an attacker arbitrary code execution. This can occur when user input is passed to code that interprets it as an expression to be evaluated, such as `eval` or `exec`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2067875Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2067968Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2068090Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2069215Z +               'Avoid including user input in any expression that may be dynamically evaluated. If user input must be included, use context-specific escaping before including it. It is important that the correct escaping is used for the type of evaluation that will occur.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2069407Z -               'Sensitive data should not be logged.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2069487Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2069572Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2069695Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2071508Z +               'The following example shows two functions setting a name from a request. The first function uses `exec` to execute the `setname` function. This is dangerous as it can allow a malicious user to execute arbitrary code on the server. For example, the user could supply the value `"\' + subprocess.call(\'rm -rf\') + \'"` to destroy the server\'s file system. The second function calls the `setname` function directly and is thus safe.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2072442Z -               'In the example the entire process environment is logged using \\`print\\`. Regular users of the production deployed application should not have access to this much information about the environment configuration.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2072528Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2072607Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2072718Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2072812Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2072949Z +               'urlpatterns = [\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2073118Z +               '    # Route to code_execution\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2073427Z +               "    url(r'^code-ex1$', code_execution_bad, name='code-execution-bad'),\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2073725Z +               "    url(r'^code-ex2$', code_execution_good, name='code-execution-good')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2074030Z +               ']\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2074131Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2074302Z +               'def code_execution(request):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2074474Z +               "    if request.method == 'POST':\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2074830Z +               "        first_name = base64.decodestring(request.POST.get('first_name', ''))\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2075055Z +               '        #BAD -- Allow user to define code to be run.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2075249Z +               `        exec("setname('%s')" % first_name)\n` +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2075509Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2075694Z +               'def code_execution(request):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2075864Z +               "    if request.method == 'POST':\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2076187Z +               "        first_name = base64.decodestring(request.POST.get('first_name', ''))\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2076367Z +               '        #GOOD --Call code directly\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2076526Z +               '        setname(first_name)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2076615Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2076813Z -               '# BAD: Logging cleartext sensitive data\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2076941Z -               'import os\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2077147Z -               'print(f"[INFO] Environment: {os.environ}")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2077236Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2077518Z -               'In the second example the data that is logged is not sensitive.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2077605Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2077741Z +               '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2078071Z +               '* OWASP: [Code Injection](https://www.owasp.org/index.php/Code_Injection).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2078543Z +               '* Wikipedia: [Code Injection](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Code_injection).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2078945Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-94](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2079328Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-95](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/95.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2079712Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-116](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/116.html).\n'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2079794Z +           },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2079933Z +           id: 'py/code-injection',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2080076Z +           name: 'py/code-injection',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2080179Z +           properties: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2080334Z +             'problem.severity': 'error',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2080486Z +             'security-severity': '9.3',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2080619Z +             'sub-severity': 'high',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2081078Z +             description: 'Interpreting unsanitized user input as code allows a malicious user to perform arbitrary\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2081240Z +               '              code execution.',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2081375Z +             id: 'py/code-injection',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2081513Z +             kind: 'path-problem',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2081650Z +             name: 'Code injection',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2081776Z +             precision: 'high',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2081872Z +             tags: [
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2081970Z +               'security',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2082110Z +               'external/cwe/cwe-094',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2082248Z +               'external/cwe/cwe-095',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2082378Z +               'external/cwe/cwe-116'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2082462Z +             ]
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2082541Z +           },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2082673Z +           shortDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2082809Z +             text: 'Code injection'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2082883Z +           }
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2082966Z +         },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2083043Z +         {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2083180Z +           defaultConfiguration: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2083292Z +             enabled: true,
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2083397Z +             level: 'error'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2083472Z +           },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2083602Z +           fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2084361Z +             text: 'Building a NoSQL query from user-controlled sources is vulnerable to insertion of malicious NoSQL code by the user.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2084451Z +           },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2084546Z +           help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2084703Z +             markdown: '# NoSQL Injection\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2086645Z +               'Passing user-controlled sources into NoSQL queries can result in a NoSQL injection flaw. This tainted NoSQL query containing a user-controlled source can then execute a malicious query in a NoSQL database such as MongoDB. In order for the user-controlled source to taint the NoSQL query, the user-controller source must be converted into a Python object using something like `json.loads` or `xmltodict.parse`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2086744Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2088108Z +               'Because a user-controlled source is passed into the query, the malicious user can have complete control over the query itself. When the tainted query is executed, the malicious user can commit malicious actions such as bypassing role restrictions or accessing and modifying restricted data in the NoSQL database.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2088208Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2088303Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2088437Z +               '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2089696Z +               "NoSQL injections can be prevented by escaping user-input's special characters that are passed into the NoSQL query from the user-supplied source. Alternatively, using a sanitize library such as MongoSanitizer will ensure that user-supplied sources can not act as a malicious query.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2089916Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2090008Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2090140Z +               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2090643Z +               'In the example below, the user-supplied source is passed to a MongoDB function that queries the MongoDB database.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2090732Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2090824Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2090936Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2091109Z +               'from flask import Flask, request\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2091288Z +               'from flask_pymongo import PyMongo\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2091418Z +               'import json\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2091505Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2091660Z +               'mongo = PyMongo(app)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2091748Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2091841Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2091979Z +               '@app.route("/")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2092116Z +               'def home_page():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2092341Z +               "    unsanitized_search = request.args['search']\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2092565Z +               '    json_search = json.loads(unsanitized_search)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2092657Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2092904Z +               "    result = mongo.db.user.find({'name': json_search})\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2092993Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2093185Z -               "not_sensitive_data = {'a': 1, 'b': 2}\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2093424Z -               '# GOOD: it is fine to log data that is not sensitive\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2093696Z -               'print(f"[INFO] Some object contains: {not_sensitive_data}")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2093977Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2094540Z +               'This can be fixed by using a sanitizer library like MongoSanitizer as shown in this annotated code version below.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2094626Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2094720Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2094846Z +               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2095013Z +               'from flask import Flask, request\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2095190Z +               'from flask_pymongo import PyMongo\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2095413Z +               'from mongosanitizer.sanitizer import sanitize\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2095535Z +               'import json\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2095629Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2095769Z +               'mongo = PyMongo(app)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2095863Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2095959Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2096089Z +               '@app.route("/")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2096372Z +               'def home_page():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2096581Z +               "    unsafe_search = request.args['search']\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2096780Z +               '    json_search = json.loads(unsafe_search)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2096999Z +               '    safe_search = sanitize(unsanitized_search)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2097088Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2097378Z +               "    result = client.db.collection.find_one({'data': safe_search})\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2097472Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2097564Z +               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2097658Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2097771Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2098036Z +               '* Mongoengine: [Documentation](http://mongoengine.org/).\n' +
