2026-10-20T21:06:14.2104406Z -               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-359](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/359.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2104795Z -               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-532](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/532.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2105041Z -             text: '# Clear-text logging of sensitive information\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2105518Z -               'If sensitive data is written to a log entry it could be exposed to an attacker who gains access to the logs.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2105599Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2106964Z +               'Because a user-controlled source is passed into the query, the malicious user can have complete control over the query itself. When the tainted query is executed, the malicious user can commit malicious actions such as bypassing role restrictions or accessing and modifying restricted data in the NoSQL database.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2107946Z -               'Potential attackers can obtain sensitive user data when the log output is displayed. Additionally that data may expose system information such as full path names, system information, and sometimes usernames and passwords.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2108031Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2108109Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2108231Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2109624Z +               "NoSQL injections can be prevented by escaping user-input's special characters that are passed into the NoSQL query from the user-supplied source. Alternatively, using a sanitize library such as MongoSanitizer will ensure that user-supplied sources can not act as a malicious query.\n" +
