2026-10-20T21:06:14.2176892Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-200](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2177139Z +             text: '# Binding a socket to all network interfaces\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2179777Z +               'Sockets can be used to communicate with other machines on a network. You can use the (IP address, port) pair to define the access restrictions for the socket you create. When using the built-in Python `socket` module (for instance, when building a message sender service or an FTP server data transmitter), one has to bind the port to some interface. When you bind the port to all interfaces using `0.0.0.0` as the IP address, you essentially allow it to accept connections from any IPv4 address provided that it can get to the socket via routing. Binding to all interfaces is therefore associated with security risks.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2180490Z -               '* PortSwigger: [Cookie without HttpOnly flag set](https://portswigger.net/kb/issues/00500600_cookie-without-httponly-flag-set)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2180907Z -               '* MDN: [Set-Cookie](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Set-Cookie).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2181327Z -               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-1004](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1004.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2181582Z -             text: '# Sensitive cookie missing `HttpOnly` attribute\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2182946Z -               'Cookies without the `HttpOnly` flag set are accessible to JavaScript running in the same origin. In case of a Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability, the cookie can be stolen by a malicious script. If a sensitive cookie does not need to be accessed directly by client-side JS, the `HttpOnly` flag should be set.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2183040Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2183128Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2183249Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2184467Z +               'Bind your service incoming traffic only to a dedicated interface. If you need to bind more than one interface using the built-in `socket` module, create multiple sockets (instead of binding to one socket to all interfaces).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2185081Z -               "Set `httponly` to `True`, or add `; HttpOnly;` to the cookie's raw header value, to ensure that the cookie is not accessible via JavaScript.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2185168Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2185256Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2185375Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2186081Z +               "In this example, two sockets are insecure because they are bound to all interfaces; one through the `0.0.0.0` notation and another one through an empty string `''`.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2186695Z -               'In the following examples, the cases marked GOOD show secure cookie attributes being set; whereas in the case marked BAD they are not set.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2186780Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2186860Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2186971Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2187237Z +               'import socket\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2187519Z -               'from flask import Flask, request, make_response, Response\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2187610Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2187793Z +               '# binds to all interfaces, insecure\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2188043Z +               's = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2188199Z +               "s.bind(('0.0.0.0', 31137))\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2188279Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2188458Z +               '# binds to all interfaces, insecure\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2188699Z +               's = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2188834Z +               "s.bind(('', 4040))\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2188982Z -               '@app.route("/good1")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2189109Z -               'def good1():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2189268Z -               '    resp = make_response()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2189838Z -               `    resp.set_cookie("sessionid", value="value", secure=True, httponly=True, samesite='Strict') # GOOD: Attributes are securely set\n` +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2190095Z -               '    return resp\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2190182Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2190399Z +               '# binds only to a dedicated interface, secure\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2190634Z +               's = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2190798Z +               "s.bind(('84.68.10.12', 8080))\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2190884Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2191024Z -               '@app.route("/good2")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2191159Z -               'def good2():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2191320Z -               '    resp = make_response()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2191850Z -               `    resp.headers['Set-Cookie'] = "sessionid=value; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Strict" # GOOD: Attributes are securely set \n` +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2191992Z -               '    return resp\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2192084Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2192230Z -               '@app.route("/bad1")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2192368Z -               'def bad1():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2192521Z -               '    resp = make_response()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2193295Z -               `    resp.set_cookie("sessionid", value="value", samesite='None') # BAD: the SameSite attribute is set to 'None' and the 'Secure' and 'HttpOnly' attributes are set to False by default.\n` +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2193432Z -               '    return resp\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2193516Z                 '```\n' +
