2026-10-20T21:06:14.2264942Z -           fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2265464Z -             text: 'Using externally controlled strings in a command line may allow a malicious user to change the meaning of the command.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2265544Z -           },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2265641Z -           help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2265823Z -             markdown: '# Uncontrolled command line\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2266496Z -               'Code that passes user input directly to `exec`, `eval`, or some other library routine that executes a command, allows the user to execute malicious code.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2266723Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2267342Z +               '* Many browsers accept backslash characters (`\\`) as equivalent to forward slash characters (`/`) in URLs, but the `urlparse` function does not.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2268114Z +               '* Mistyped URLs such as `https:/example.com` or `https:///example.com` are parsed as having an empty `netloc` attribute, while browsers will still redirect to the correct site.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2268201Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2268338Z -               '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2269417Z -               'If possible, use hard-coded string literals to specify the command to run or the library to load. Instead of passing the user input directly to the process or library function, examine the user input and then choose among hard-coded string literals.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2269512Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2270174Z -               'If the applicable libraries or commands cannot be determined at compile time, then add code to verify that the user input string is safe before using it.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2270273Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2270368Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2270489Z -               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2271633Z -               'The following example shows two functions. The first is unsafe as it takes a shell script that can be changed by a user, and passes it straight to `subprocess.call()` without examining it first. The second is safe as it selects the command from a predefined allowlist.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2271730Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2271818Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2271931Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2272143Z +               'from flask import Flask, request, redirect\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2272325Z +               'from urllib.parse import urlparse\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2272408Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2272556Z +               'app = Flask(__name__)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2272696Z -               'urlpatterns = [\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2272874Z -               '    # Route to command_execution\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2273250Z -               "    url(r'^command-ex1$', command_execution_unsafe, name='command-execution-unsafe'),\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2273603Z -               "    url(r'^command-ex2$', command_execution_safe, name='command-execution-safe')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2273738Z -               ']\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2274025Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2274183Z +               "@app.route('/')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2274317Z +               'def hello():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2274519Z +               "    target = request.args.get('target', '')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2274888Z +               "    target = target.replace('\\\\', '')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2275192Z +               '    if not urlparse(target).netloc and not urlparse(target).scheme:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2275398Z +               '        # relative path, safe to redirect\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2275587Z +               '        return redirect(target, code=302)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2275826Z +               '    # ignore the target and redirect to the home page\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2276010Z +               "    return redirect('/', code=302)\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2276146Z -               'COMMANDS = {\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2276281Z -               '    "list" :"ls",\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2276424Z -               '    "stat" : "stat"\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2276522Z -               '}\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2276602Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2276801Z -               'def command_execution_unsafe(request):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2276984Z -               "    if request.method == 'POST':\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2277199Z -               "        action = request.POST.get('action', '')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2277398Z -               '        #BAD -- No sanitizing of input\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2277741Z -               '        subprocess.call(["application", action])\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2277837Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2278027Z -               'def command_execution_safe(request):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2278196Z -               "    if request.method == 'POST':\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2278404Z -               "        action = request.POST.get('action', '')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2278581Z -               '        #GOOD -- Use an allowlist\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2278835Z -               '        subprocess.call(["application", COMMANDS[action]])\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2278932Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2279023Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2279730Z +               'For Django application, you can use the function `url_has_allowed_host_and_scheme` to check that a URL is safe to redirect to, as shown in the following example:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2279821Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2279954Z -               '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2280330Z -               '* OWASP: [Command Injection](https://www.owasp.org/index.php/Command_Injection).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2280732Z -               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-78](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2281121Z -               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-88](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/88.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2281304Z -             text: '# Uncontrolled command line\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2281972Z -               'Code that passes user input directly to `exec`, `eval`, or some other library routine that executes a command, allows the user to execute malicious code.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2282052Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2282155Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2282298Z -               '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2283371Z -               'If possible, use hard-coded string literals to specify the command to run or the library to load. Instead of passing the user input directly to the process or library function, examine the user input and then choose among hard-coded string literals.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2283473Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2284405Z -               'If the applicable libraries or commands cannot be determined at compile time, then add code to verify that the user input string is safe before using it.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2284502Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2284599Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2284731Z -               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2286009Z -               'The following example shows two functions. The first is unsafe as it takes a shell script that can be changed by a user, and passes it straight to `subprocess.call()` without examining it first. The second is safe as it selects the command from a predefined allowlist.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2286113Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2286214Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2286320Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2286551Z +               'from django.http import HttpResponseRedirect\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2286749Z +               'from django.shortcuts import redirect\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2287033Z +               'from django.utils.http import url_has_allowed_host_and_scheme\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2287202Z +               'from django.views import View\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2287282Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2287445Z +               'class RedirectView(View):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2287653Z +               '    def get(self, request, *args, **kwargs):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2287858Z +               "        target = request.GET.get('target', '')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2288170Z +               '        if url_has_allowed_host_and_scheme(target, allowed_hosts=None):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2288386Z +               '            return HttpResponseRedirect(target)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2288640Z +               '        else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2288891Z +               '            # ignore the target and redirect to the home page\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2289061Z +               "            return redirect('/')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2289157Z +               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2289681Z +               'Note that `url_has_allowed_host_and_scheme` handles backslashes correctly, so no additional processing is required.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2289822Z -               'urlpatterns = [\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2289991Z -               '    # Route to command_execution\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2290374Z -               "    url(r'^command-ex1$', command_execution_unsafe, name='command-execution-unsafe'),\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2290734Z -               "    url(r'^command-ex2$', command_execution_safe, name='command-execution-safe')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2290828Z -               ']\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2290915Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2291041Z -               'COMMANDS = {\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2291179Z -               '    "list" :"ls",\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2291324Z -               '    "stat" : "stat"\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2291416Z -               '}\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2291501Z                 '\n' +
