2026-10-20T21:06:14.2303494Z -           },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2303591Z -           help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2304002Z -             markdown: '# Server Side Template Injection\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2304949Z -               'A template from a server templating engine such as Jinja constructed from user input can allow the user to execute arbitrary code using certain template features. It can also allow for cross-site scripting.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2305040Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2305120Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2305244Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2306300Z +               'To guard against untrusted URL redirection, it is advisable to avoid putting user input directly into a redirect URL. Instead, maintain a list of authorized redirects on the server; then choose from that list based on the user input provided.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2307601Z -               'Ensure that an untrusted value is not used to directly construct a template. Jinja also provides `SandboxedEnvironment` that prohibits access to unsafe methods and attributes. This can be used if constructing a template from user input is absolutely necessary.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2307699Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2308435Z +               'If this is not possible, then the user input should be validated in some other way, for example, by verifying that the target URL does not include an explicit host name.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2308515Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2308611Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2308729Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2309426Z +               'The following example shows an HTTP request parameter being used directly in a URL redirect without validating the input, which facilitates phishing attacks:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2309953Z -               'In the following case, `template` is used to generate a Jinja2 template string. This can lead to remote code execution.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2310042Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2310120Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2310232Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2310562Z +               'from flask import Flask, request, redirect\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2310730Z -               'from django.urls import path\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2310921Z -               'from django.http import HttpResponse\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2311110Z -               'from jinja2 import Template, escape\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2311191Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2311342Z +               'app = Flask(__name__)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2311421Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2311563Z +               "@app.route('/')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2311695Z +               'def hello():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2311893Z +               "    target = request.args.get('target', '')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2312078Z +               '    return redirect(target, code=302)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2312219Z -               'def a(request):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2312405Z -               "    template = request.GET['template']\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2312491Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2312734Z -               '    # BAD: Template is constructed from user input. \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2312889Z -               '    t = Template(template)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2312996Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2313167Z -               "    name = request.GET['name']\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2313354Z -               '    html = t.render(name=escape(name))\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2313532Z -               '    return HttpResponse(html)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2313621Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2313717Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2314067Z -               'urlpatterns = [\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2314211Z -               "    path('a', a),\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2314310Z -               ']\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2314399Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2314999Z +               'If you know the set of valid redirect targets, you can maintain a list of them on the server and check that the user input is in that list:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2315530Z -               'The following is an example of a string that could be used to cause remote code execution when interpreted as a template:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2315611Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2315698Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2315804Z -               '```txt\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2316527Z -               `{% for s in ().__class__.__base__.__subclasses__() %}{% if "warning" in s.__name__ %}{{s()._module.__builtins__['__import__']('os').system('cat /etc/passwd') }}{% endif %}{% endfor %}\n` +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2316623Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2316722Z -               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2317521Z -               'In the following case, user input is not used to construct the template. Instead, it is only used as the parameters to render the template, which is safe.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2317625Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2317722Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2317832Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2318043Z +               'from flask import Flask, request, redirect\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2318212Z -               'from django.urls import path\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2318396Z -               'from django.http import HttpResponse\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2318584Z -               'from jinja2 import Template, escape\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2318665Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2318977Z +               'VALID_REDIRECT = "http://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/601.html"\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2319063Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2319212Z +               'app = Flask(__name__)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2319351Z -               'def a(request):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2319654Z -               '    # GOOD: Template is a constant, not constructed from user input\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2319832Z -               '    t = Template("Hello, {{name}}!")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2319917Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2320182Z +               "@app.route('/')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2320308Z +               'def hello():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2320514Z +               "    target = request.args.get('target', '')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2320684Z +               '    if target == VALID_REDIRECT:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2320882Z +               '        return redirect(target, code=302)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2321004Z +               '    else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2321246Z +               '        # ignore the target and redirect to the home page\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2321432Z +               "        return redirect('/', code=302)\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2321602Z -               "    name = request.GET['name']\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2321781Z -               '    html = t.render(name=escape(name))\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2321954Z -               '    return HttpResponse(html)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2322040Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2322128Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2322269Z -               'urlpatterns = [\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2322401Z -               "    path('a', a),\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2322501Z -               ']\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2322587Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2323758Z +               'Often this is not possible, so an alternative is to check that the target URL does not specify an explicit host name. For example, you can use the `urlparse` function from the Python standard library to parse the URL and check that the `netloc` attribute is empty.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2324415Z -               'In the following case, a `SandboxedEnvironment` is used, preventing remote code execution.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2324503Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2325174Z +               'Note, however, that some cases are not handled as we desire out-of-the-box by `urlparse`, so we need to adjust two things, as shown in the example below:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2325261Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2325890Z +               '* Many browsers accept backslash characters (`\\`) as equivalent to forward slash characters (`/`) in URLs, but the `urlparse` function does not.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2326653Z +               '* Mistyped URLs such as `https:/example.com` or `https:///example.com` are parsed as having an empty `netloc` attribute, while browsers will still redirect to the correct site.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2326778Z -               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2326949Z -               'from django.urls import path\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2327135Z -               'from django.http import HttpResponse\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2327300Z -               'from jinja2 import escape\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2327534Z -               'from jinja2.sandbox import SandboxedEnvironment\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2327755Z                 '\n' +
