2026-10-20T21:06:14.2345577Z -               ']\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2345664Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2346383Z +               'For Django application, you can use the function `url_has_allowed_host_and_scheme` to check that a URL is safe to redirect to, as shown in the following example:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2346932Z -               'The following is an example of a string that could be used to cause remote code execution when interpreted as a template:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2347017Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2347103Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2347208Z -               '```txt\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2347998Z -               `{% for s in ().__class__.__base__.__subclasses__() %}{% if "warning" in s.__name__ %}{{s()._module.__builtins__['__import__']('os').system('cat /etc/passwd') }}{% endif %}{% endfor %}\n` +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2348099Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2348193Z -               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2348871Z -               'In the following case, user input is not used to construct the template. Instead, it is only used as the parameters to render the template, which is safe.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2348969Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2349058Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2349173Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2349406Z +               'from django.http import HttpResponseRedirect\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2349601Z +               'from django.shortcuts import redirect\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2349890Z +               'from django.utils.http import url_has_allowed_host_and_scheme\n' +
