2026-10-20T21:06:14.2426670Z             fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2427351Z +             text: 'Matching a URL or hostname against a regular expression that contains an unescaped dot as part of the hostname might match more hostnames than expected.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2427872Z -             text: 'Building an LDAP query from user-controlled sources is vulnerable to insertion of malicious LDAP code by the user.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2427950Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2428041Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2428297Z +             markdown: '# Incomplete regular expression for hostnames\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2429224Z +               'Sanitizing untrusted URLs is a common technique for preventing attacks such as request forgeries and malicious redirections. Often, this is done by checking that the host of a URL is in a set of allowed hosts.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2429488Z -             markdown: '# LDAP query built from user-controlled sources\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2430491Z -               'If an LDAP query or DN is built using string concatenation or string formatting, and the components of the concatenation include user input without any proper sanitization, a user is likely to be able to run malicious LDAP queries.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2430580Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2432089Z +               'If a regular expression implements such a check, it is easy to accidentally make the check too permissive by not escaping the `.` meta-characters appropriately. Even if the check is not used in a security-critical context, the incomplete check may still cause undesirable behaviors when it accidentally succeeds.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2432189Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2432280Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2432403Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2433099Z +               'Escape all meta-characters appropriately when constructing regular expressions for security checks, and pay special attention to the `.` meta-character.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2435905Z -               'If user input must be included in an LDAP query or DN, it should be escaped to avoid a malicious user providing special characters that change the meaning of the query. In Python2, user input should be escaped with `ldap.dn.escape_dn_chars` or `ldap.filter.escape_filter_chars`, while in Python3, user input should be escaped with `ldap3.utils.dn.escape_rdn` or `ldap3.utils.conv.escape_filter_chars` depending on the component tainted by the user. A good practice is to escape filter characters that could change the meaning of the query (https://tools.ietf.org/search/rfc4515\\#section-3).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2436163Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2436250Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2436359Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2436896Z +               'The following example code checks that a URL redirection will reach the `example.com` domain, or one of its subdomains.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2437473Z -               'In the following examples, the code accepts both `username` and `dc` from the user, which it then uses to build a LDAP query and DN.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2437554Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2438719Z -               'The first and the second example uses the unsanitized user input directly in the search filter and DN for the LDAP query. A malicious user could provide special characters to change the meaning of these components, and search for a completely different set of values.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2438807Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2438897Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2439012Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2439221Z +               'from flask import Flask, request, redirect\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2439339Z +               'import re\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2439517Z -               'from flask import request, Flask\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2439651Z -               'import ldap\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2439732Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2439887Z +               'app = Flask(__name__)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2439966Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2440212Z +               'UNSAFE_REGEX = re.compile("(www|beta).example.com/")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2440464Z +               'SAFE_REGEX = re.compile(r"(www|beta)\\.example\\.com/")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2440610Z -               '@app.route("/normal")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2440749Z -               'def normal():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2440930Z -               "    unsafe_dc = request.args['dc']\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2441130Z -               "    unsafe_filter = request.args['username']\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2441219Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2441391Z +               "@app.route('/some/path/bad')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2441535Z +               'def unsafe(request):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2441739Z +               "    target = request.args.get('target', '')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2441914Z +               '    if UNSAFE_REGEX.match(target):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2442086Z +               '        return redirect(target)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2442256Z -               '    dn = "dc={}".format(unsafe_dc)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2442487Z -               '    search_filter = "(user={})".format(unsafe_filter)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2442574Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2442744Z +               "@app.route('/some/path/good')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2443016Z +               'def safe(request):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2443224Z +               "    target = request.args.get('target', '')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2443403Z +               '    if SAFE_REGEX.match(target):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2443567Z +               '        return redirect(target)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2444076Z -               '    ldap_connection = ldap.initialize("ldap://127.0.0.1")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2444270Z -               '    user = ldap_connection.search_s(\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2444487Z -               '        dn, ldap.SCOPE_SUBTREE, search_filter)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2444573Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2444656Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2445567Z +               'The `unsafe` check is easy to bypass because the unescaped `.` allows for any character before `example.com`, effectively allowing the redirect to go to an attacker-controlled domain such as `wwwXexample.com`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2445654Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2446173Z +               'The `safe` check closes this vulnerability by escaping the `.` so that URLs of the form `wwwXexample.com` are rejected.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2446484Z -               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2446670Z -               'from flask import request, Flask\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2446800Z -               'import ldap3\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2446887Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2446971Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2447100Z +               '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2447459Z +               '* OWASP: [SSRF](https://www.owasp.org/index.php/Server_Side_Request_Forgery)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2448214Z +               '* OWASP: [XSS Unvalidated Redirects and Forwards Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Unvalidated_Redirects_and_Forwards_Cheat_Sheet.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2448611Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-20](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2448852Z +             text: '# Incomplete regular expression for hostnames\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2449775Z +               'Sanitizing untrusted URLs is a common technique for preventing attacks such as request forgeries and malicious redirections. Often, this is done by checking that the host of a URL is in a set of allowed hosts.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2449934Z -               '@app.route("/normal")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2450073Z -               'def normal():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2450250Z -               "    unsafe_dc = request.args['dc']\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2450462Z -               "    unsafe_filter = request.args['username']\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2450552Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2451904Z +               'If a regular expression implements such a check, it is easy to accidentally make the check too permissive by not escaping the `.` meta-characters appropriately. Even if the check is not used in a security-critical context, the incomplete check may still cause undesirable behaviors when it accidentally succeeds.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2452080Z -               '    dn = "dc={}".format(unsafe_dc)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2452319Z -               '    search_filter = "(user={})".format(unsafe_filter)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2452403Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2452603Z -               "    srv = ldap3.Server('ldap://127.0.0.1')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2452856Z -               '    conn = ldap3.Connection(srv, user=dn, auto_bind=True)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2453028Z -               '    conn.search(dn, search_filter)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2453114Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2453215Z -               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2454455Z -               'In the third and fourth example, the input provided by the user is sanitized before it is included in the search filter or DN. This ensures the meaning of the query cannot be changed by a malicious user.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2454563Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2454823Z -               '\n' +
