2026-10-20T21:06:14.2467359Z -               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-90](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/90.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2467595Z -             text: '# LDAP query built from user-controlled sources\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2468605Z -               'If an LDAP query or DN is built using string concatenation or string formatting, and the components of the concatenation include user input without any proper sanitization, a user is likely to be able to run malicious LDAP queries.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2468836Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2468926Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2469055Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2469752Z +               'Escape all meta-characters appropriately when constructing regular expressions for security checks, and pay special attention to the `.` meta-character.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2472333Z -               'If user input must be included in an LDAP query or DN, it should be escaped to avoid a malicious user providing special characters that change the meaning of the query. In Python2, user input should be escaped with `ldap.dn.escape_dn_chars` or `ldap.filter.escape_filter_chars`, while in Python3, user input should be escaped with `ldap3.utils.dn.escape_rdn` or `ldap3.utils.conv.escape_filter_chars` depending on the component tainted by the user. A good practice is to escape filter characters that could change the meaning of the query (https://tools.ietf.org/search/rfc4515\\#section-3).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2472426Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2472511Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2472627Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2473159Z +               'The following example code checks that a URL redirection will reach the `example.com` domain, or one of its subdomains.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2473735Z -               'In the following examples, the code accepts both `username` and `dc` from the user, which it then uses to build a LDAP query and DN.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2474049Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2475254Z -               'The first and the second example uses the unsanitized user input directly in the search filter and DN for the LDAP query. A malicious user could provide special characters to change the meaning of these components, and search for a completely different set of values.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2475348Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2475448Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2475560Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2475770Z +               'from flask import Flask, request, redirect\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2475888Z +               'import re\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2476065Z -               'from flask import request, Flask\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2476197Z -               'import ldap\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2476276Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2476429Z +               'app = Flask(__name__)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2476512Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2476752Z +               'UNSAFE_REGEX = re.compile("(www|beta).example.com/")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2477215Z +               'SAFE_REGEX = re.compile(r"(www|beta)\\.example\\.com/")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2477378Z -               '@app.route("/normal")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2477513Z -               'def normal():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2477692Z -               "    unsafe_dc = request.args['dc']\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2477895Z -               "    unsafe_filter = request.args['username']\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2477982Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2478152Z +               "@app.route('/some/path/bad')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2478294Z +               'def unsafe(request):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2478502Z +               "    target = request.args.get('target', '')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2478684Z +               '    if UNSAFE_REGEX.match(target):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2478850Z +               '        return redirect(target)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2479022Z -               '    dn = "dc={}".format(unsafe_dc)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2479262Z -               '    search_filter = "(user={})".format(unsafe_filter)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2479342Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2479512Z +               "@app.route('/some/path/good')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2479789Z +               'def safe(request):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2479994Z +               "    target = request.args.get('target', '')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2480166Z +               '    if SAFE_REGEX.match(target):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2480331Z +               '        return redirect(target)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2480593Z -               '    ldap_connection = ldap.initialize("ldap://127.0.0.1")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2480779Z -               '    user = ldap_connection.search_s(\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2480984Z -               '        dn, ldap.SCOPE_SUBTREE, search_filter)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2481070Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2481158Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2482072Z +               'The `unsafe` check is easy to bypass because the unescaped `.` allows for any character before `example.com`, effectively allowing the redirect to go to an attacker-controlled domain such as `wwwXexample.com`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2482161Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2482679Z +               'The `safe` check closes this vulnerability by escaping the `.` so that URLs of the form `wwwXexample.com` are rejected.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2482800Z -               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2482973Z -               'from flask import request, Flask\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2483110Z -               'import ldap3\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2483189Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2483274Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2483417Z -               '@app.route("/normal")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2483549Z -               'def normal():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2483722Z -               "    unsafe_dc = request.args['dc']\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2484193Z -               "    unsafe_filter = request.args['username']\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2484299Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2484470Z -               '    dn = "dc={}".format(unsafe_dc)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2484700Z -               '    search_filter = "(user={})".format(unsafe_filter)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2484799Z -               '\n' +
