2026-10-20T21:06:14.2641476Z +               'Another common problem is failing to escape the dash character in a regular expression. An unescaped dash is interpreted as part of a range. For example, in the character class `[a-zA-Z0-9%=.,-_]` the last character range matches the 55 characters between `,` and `_` (both included), which overlaps with the range `[0-9]` and is clearly not intended by the writer.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2642404Z -               'Many cryptographic algorithms are known to be weak or flawed. The security guarantees of a system often rely on the underlying cryptography, so using a weak algorithm can have severe consequences. For example:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2642489Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2642894Z -               '* If a weak encryption algorithm is used, an attacker may be able to decrypt sensitive data.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2643462Z -               '* If a weak algorithm is used for digital signatures, an attacker may be able to forge signatures and impersonate legitimate users.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2644719Z -               'This query alerts on any use of a weak cryptographic algorithm that is not a hashing algorithm. Use of broken or weak cryptographic hash functions are handled by the `py/weak-sensitive-data-hashing` query.\n' +
