2026-10-20T21:06:14.2751284Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2751363Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2751653Z +             markdown: '# Accepting unknown SSH host keys when using Paramiko\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2752447Z +               'In the Secure Shell (SSH) protocol, host keys are used to verify the identity of remote hosts. Accepting unknown host keys may leave the connection open to man-in-the-middle attacks.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2752644Z -             markdown: '# Failure to use secure cookies\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2754120Z -               "Cookies without the `Secure` flag set may be transmitted using HTTP instead of HTTPS. This leaves them vulnerable to being read by a third party attacker. If a sensitive cookie such as a session key is intercepted this way, it would allow the attacker to perform actions on a user's behalf.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2754217Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2754435Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2754566Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2756090Z +               'Do not accept unknown host keys. In particular, do not set the default missing host key policy for the Paramiko library to either `AutoAddPolicy` or `WarningPolicy`. Both of these policies continue even when the host key is unknown. The default setting of `RejectPolicy` is secure because it throws an exception when it encounters an unknown host key.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2756697Z -               "Always set `secure` to `True`, or add `; Secure;` to the cookie's raw header value, to ensure SSL is used to transmit the cookie with encryption.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2756790Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2756878Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2756985Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2758808Z +               'The following example shows two ways of opening an SSH connection to `example.com`. The first function sets the missing host key policy to `AutoAddPolicy`. If the host key verification fails, the client will continue to interact with the server, even though the connection may be compromised. The second function sets the host key policy to `RejectPolicy`, and will throw an exception if the host key verification fails.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2759549Z -               'In the following examples, the cases marked GOOD show secure cookie attributes being set; whereas in the case marked BAD they are not set.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2759630Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2759713Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2759822Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2760127Z +               'from paramiko.client import SSHClient, AutoAddPolicy, RejectPolicy\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2760392Z -               'from flask import Flask, request, make_response, Response\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2760476Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2760621Z +               'def unsafe_connect():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2760779Z +               '    client = SSHClient()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2761028Z +               '    client.set_missing_host_key_policy(AutoAddPolicy)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2761213Z +               '    client.connect("example.com")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2761300Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2761465Z +               '    # ... interaction with server\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2761620Z -               '@app.route("/good1")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2761757Z -               'def good1():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2761919Z -               '    resp = make_response()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2762492Z -               `    resp.set_cookie("sessionid", value="value", secure=True, httponly=True, samesite='Strict') # GOOD: Attributes are securely set\n` +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2762631Z -               '    return resp\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2762711Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2762855Z +               '    client.close()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2762943Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2763086Z +               'def safe_connect():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2763241Z +               '    client = SSHClient()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2763480Z +               '    client.set_missing_host_key_policy(RejectPolicy)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2763654Z +               '    client.connect("example.com")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2764013Z -               '@app.route("/good2")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2764162Z -               'def good2():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2764323Z -               '    resp = make_response()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2764858Z -               `    resp.headers['Set-Cookie'] = "sessionid=value; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Strict" # GOOD: Attributes are securely set \n` +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2764988Z -               '    return resp\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2765072Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2765246Z +               '    # ... interaction with server\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2765339Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2765631Z +               '    client.close()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2765734Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2765874Z -               '@app.route("/bad1")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2766008Z -               'def bad1():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2766162Z -               '    resp = make_response()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2766933Z -               `    resp.set_cookie("sessionid", value="value", samesite='None') # BAD: the SameSite attribute is set to 'None' and the 'Secure' and 'HttpOnly' attributes are set to False by default.\n` +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2767072Z -               '    return resp\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2767156Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2767241Z                 '\n' +
