2026-10-20T21:06:14.2771116Z -               '* PortSwigger: [TLS cookie without secure flag set](https://portswigger.net/kb/issues/00500200_tls-cookie-without-secure-flag-set).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2771530Z -               '* MDN: [Set-Cookie](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Set-Cookie).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2771938Z -               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-614](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/614.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2772134Z -             text: '# Failure to use secure cookies\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2773388Z -               "Cookies without the `Secure` flag set may be transmitted using HTTP instead of HTTPS. This leaves them vulnerable to being read by a third party attacker. If a sensitive cookie such as a session key is intercepted this way, it would allow the attacker to perform actions on a user's behalf.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2773476Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2773559Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2773678Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2775503Z +               'Do not accept unknown host keys. In particular, do not set the default missing host key policy for the Paramiko library to either `AutoAddPolicy` or `WarningPolicy`. Both of these policies continue even when the host key is unknown. The default setting of `RejectPolicy` is secure because it throws an exception when it encounters an unknown host key.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2776116Z -               "Always set `secure` to `True`, or add `; Secure;` to the cookie's raw header value, to ensure SSL is used to transmit the cookie with encryption.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2776207Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2776285Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2776407Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2778225Z +               'The following example shows two ways of opening an SSH connection to `example.com`. The first function sets the missing host key policy to `AutoAddPolicy`. If the host key verification fails, the client will continue to interact with the server, even though the connection may be compromised. The second function sets the host key policy to `RejectPolicy`, and will throw an exception if the host key verification fails.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2778987Z -               'In the following examples, the cases marked GOOD show secure cookie attributes being set; whereas in the case marked BAD they are not set.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2779082Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2779170Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2779277Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2779591Z +               'from paramiko.client import SSHClient, AutoAddPolicy, RejectPolicy\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2779850Z -               'from flask import Flask, request, make_response, Response\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2779938Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2780092Z +               'def unsafe_connect():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2780240Z +               '    client = SSHClient()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2780485Z +               '    client.set_missing_host_key_policy(AutoAddPolicy)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2780666Z +               '    client.connect("example.com")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2780746Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2780915Z +               '    # ... interaction with server\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2781072Z -               '@app.route("/good1")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2781201Z -               'def good1():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2781361Z -               '    resp = make_response()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2782052Z -               `    resp.set_cookie("sessionid", value="value", secure=True, httponly=True, samesite='Strict') # GOOD: Attributes are securely set\n` +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2782185Z -               '    return resp\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2782269Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2782407Z +               '    client.close()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2782494Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2782653Z +               'def safe_connect():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2782806Z +               '    client = SSHClient()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2783042Z +               '    client.set_missing_host_key_policy(RejectPolicy)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2783218Z +               '    client.connect("example.com")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2783364Z -               '@app.route("/good2")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2783500Z -               'def good2():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2783656Z -               '    resp = make_response()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2784426Z -               `    resp.headers['Set-Cookie'] = "sessionid=value; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Strict" # GOOD: Attributes are securely set \n` +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2784566Z -               '    return resp\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2784647Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2784820Z +               '    # ... interaction with server\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2784913Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2785049Z +               '    client.close()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2785144Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2785285Z -               '@app.route("/bad1")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2785407Z -               'def bad1():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2785566Z -               '    resp = make_response()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2786343Z -               `    resp.set_cookie("sessionid", value="value", samesite='None') # BAD: the SameSite attribute is set to 'None' and the 'Secure' and 'HttpOnly' attributes are set to False by default.\n` +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2786472Z -               '    return resp\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2786565Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2786643Z                 '\n' +
