2026-10-20T21:06:14.2796242Z             fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2796734Z +             text: 'Running a Flask app in debug mode may allow an attacker to run arbitrary code through the Werkzeug debugger.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2797136Z -             text: 'Security checks on the substrings of an unparsed URL are often vulnerable to bypassing.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2797221Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2797301Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2797507Z +             markdown: '# Flask app is run in debug mode\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2798042Z +               'Running a Flask application with debug mode enabled may allow an attacker to gain access through the Werkzeug debugger.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2798268Z -             markdown: '# Incomplete URL substring sanitization\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2799204Z -               'Sanitizing untrusted URLs is a common technique for preventing attacks such as request forgeries and malicious redirections. Usually, this is done by checking that the host of a URL is in a set of allowed hosts.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2799292Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2800468Z -               'However, treating the URL as a string and checking if one of the allowed hosts is a substring of the URL is very prone to errors. Malicious URLs can bypass such security checks by embedding one of the allowed hosts in an unexpected location.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2800563Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2801311Z -               'Even if the substring check is not used in a security-critical context, the incomplete check may still cause undesirable behaviors when the check succeeds accidentally.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2801408Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2801500Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2801624Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2802051Z +               'Ensure that Flask applications that are run in a production environment have debugging disabled.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2802629Z -               'Parse a URL before performing a check on its host value, and ensure that the check handles arbitrary subdomain sequences correctly.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2802719Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2802797Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2803043Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2804178Z +               'Running the following code starts a Flask webserver that has debugging enabled. By visiting `/crash`, it is possible to gain access to the debugger, and run arbitrary code through the interactive debugger.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2804600Z -               'The following example code checks that a URL redirection will reach the `example.com` domain.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2804688Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2804771Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2804877Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2805041Z +               'from flask import Flask\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2805252Z -               'from flask import Flask, request, redirect\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2805435Z -               'from urllib.parse import urlparse\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2805525Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2805650Z                 'app = Flask(__name__)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2805735Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2805888Z +               "@app.route('/crash')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2806015Z +               'def main():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2806163Z +               '    raise Exception()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2806452Z -               '# Not safe, as "evil-example.net/example.com" would be accepted\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2806532Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2806677Z +               'app.run(debug=True)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2806849Z -               "@app.route('/some/path/bad1')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2806992Z -               'def unsafe1(request):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2807199Z -               "    target = request.args.get('target', '')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2807366Z -               '    if "example.com" in target:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2807538Z -               '        return redirect(target)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2807624Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2807717Z +               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2808036Z -               '# Not safe, as "benign-looking-prefix-example.com" would be accepted\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2808127Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2808265Z +               '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2808738Z +               '* Flask Quickstart Documentation: [Debug Mode](http://flask.pocoo.org/docs/1.0/quickstart/#debug-mode).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2809180Z +               '* Werkzeug Documentation: [Debugging Applications](http://werkzeug.pocoo.org/docs/0.14/debug/).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2809580Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-215](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/215.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2809977Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-489](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/489.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2810310Z +             text: '# Flask app is run in debug mode\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2810844Z +               'Running a Flask application with debug mode enabled may allow an attacker to gain access through the Werkzeug debugger.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2811169Z -               "@app.route('/some/path/bad2')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2811415Z -               'def unsafe2(request):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2811621Z -               "    target = request.args.get('target', '')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2811818Z -               '    if target.endswith("example.com"):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2811982Z -               '        return redirect(target)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2812069Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2812154Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2812291Z +               '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2812721Z +               'Ensure that Flask applications that are run in a production environment have debugging disabled.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2812805Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2813051Z -               '#Simplest and safest approach is to use an allowlist\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2813137Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2813265Z +               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2814594Z +               'Running the following code starts a Flask webserver that has debugging enabled. By visiting `/crash`, it is possible to gain access to the debugger, and run arbitrary code through the interactive debugger.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2814785Z -               "@app.route('/some/path/good1')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2814940Z -               'def safe1(request):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2815074Z -               '    allowlist = [\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2815237Z -               '        "example.com/home",\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2815395Z -               '        "example.com/login",\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2815502Z -               '    ]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2815706Z -               "    target = request.args.get('target', '')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2815870Z -               '    if target in allowlist:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2816041Z -               '        return redirect(target)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2816128Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2816333Z -               '#More complex example allowing sub-domains.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2816420Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2816547Z +               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2816697Z +               'from flask import Flask\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2816870Z -               "@app.route('/some/path/good2')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2817012Z -               'def safe2(request):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2817213Z -               "    target = request.args.get('target', '')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2817397Z -               '    host = urlparse(target).hostname\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2817583Z -               "    #Note the '.' preceding example.com\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2817804Z -               '    if host and host.endswith(".example.com"):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2817978Z -               '        return redirect(target)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2818058Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2818209Z +               'app = Flask(__name__)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2818297Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2818442Z +               "@app.route('/crash')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2818575Z +               'def main():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2818716Z +               '    raise Exception()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2818817Z -               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2819707Z -               'The first two examples show unsafe checks that are easily bypassed. In `unsafe1` the attacker can simply add `example.com` anywhere in the url. For example, `http://evil-example.net/example.com`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2819794Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2819943Z +               'app.run(debug=True)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2820761Z -               'In `unsafe2` the attacker must use a hostname ending in `example.com`, but that is easy to do. For example, `http://benign-looking-prefix-example.com`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2820849Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2820955Z +               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2821657Z -               'The second two examples show safe checks. In `safe1`, an allowlist is used. Although fairly inflexible, this is easy to get right and is most likely to be safe.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2821744Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2822255Z -               'In `safe2`, `urlparse` is used to parse the URL, then the hostname is checked to make sure it ends with `.example.com`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2822352Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2822444Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2822561Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2823034Z +               '* Flask Quickstart Documentation: [Debug Mode](http://flask.pocoo.org/docs/1.0/quickstart/#debug-mode).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2823469Z +               '* Werkzeug Documentation: [Debugging Applications](http://werkzeug.pocoo.org/docs/0.14/debug/).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2824106Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-215](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/215.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2824510Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-489](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/489.html).\n'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2824739Z +           },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2824880Z +           id: 'py/flask-debug',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2825010Z +           name: 'py/flask-debug',
