2026-10-20T21:06:14.2884571Z +             markdown: '# Regular expression injection\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2885981Z +               'Constructing a regular expression with unsanitized user input is dangerous as a malicious user may be able to modify the meaning of the expression. In particular, such a user may be able to provide a regular expression fragment that takes exponential time in the worst case, and use that to perform a Denial of Service attack.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2886248Z -             markdown: '# Incomplete regular expression for hostnames\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2887170Z -               'Sanitizing untrusted URLs is a common technique for preventing attacks such as request forgeries and malicious redirections. Often, this is done by checking that the host of a URL is in a set of allowed hosts.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2887266Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2888624Z -               'If a regular expression implements such a check, it is easy to accidentally make the check too permissive by not escaping the `.` meta-characters appropriately. Even if the check is not used in a security-critical context, the incomplete check may still cause undesirable behaviors when it accidentally succeeds.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2888719Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2888818Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2888940Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2889808Z +               "Before embedding user input into a regular expression, use a sanitization function such as `re.escape` to escape meta-characters that have a special meaning regarding regular expressions' syntax.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2890502Z -               'Escape all meta-characters appropriately when constructing regular expressions for security checks, and pay special attention to the `.` meta-character.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2890587Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2890679Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2890795Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2891131Z +               'The following examples are based on a simple Flask web server environment.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2891667Z -               'The following example code checks that a URL redirection will reach the `example.com` domain, or one of its subdomains.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2891754Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2892318Z +               'The following example shows a HTTP request parameter that is used to construct a regular expression without sanitizing it first:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2892554Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2892656Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.2892762Z                 '```python\n' +
