2026-10-20T21:06:14.3032116Z +             text: "# 'input' function used in Python 2\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3032899Z +               'In Python 2, a call to the `input()` function, `input(prompt)` is equivalent to `eval(raw_input(prompt))`. Evaluating user input without any checking can be a serious security flaw.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3033271Z -               '* Wikipedia - [Session Fixation](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Session_fixation).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3033662Z -               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-20](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3034348Z -             text: '# Construction of a cookie using user-supplied input\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3036296Z -               "Constructing cookies from user input can allow an attacker to control a user's cookie. This may lead to a session fixation attack. Additionally, client code may not expect a cookie to contain attacker-controlled data, and fail to sanitize it for common vulnerabilities such as Cross Site Scripting (XSS). An attacker manipulating the raw cookie header may additionally be able to set cookie attributes such as `HttpOnly` to insecure values.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3036393Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3036479Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3036600Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3037409Z +               'Get user input with `raw_input(prompt)` and then validate that input before evaluating. If the expected input is a number or string, then `ast.literal_eval()` can always be used safely.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3037639Z -               'Do not use raw user input to construct cookies.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3037719Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3037803Z                 '\n' +
