2026-10-20T21:06:14.3086308Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3086426Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3086800Z +               '* OWASP: [Log Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Log_Injection).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3087205Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-117](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/117.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3087353Z +             text: '# Log Injection\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3087826Z +               'If unsanitized user input is written to a log entry, a malicious user may be able to forge new log entries.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3088212Z -               '* SecLists.org: [HTTP response splitting](https://seclists.org/bugtraq/2005/Apr/187).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3088651Z -               '* OWASP: [HTTP Response Splitting](https://www.owasp.org/index.php/HTTP_Response_Splitting).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3089098Z -               '* Wikipedia: [HTTP response splitting](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTTP_response_splitting).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3089540Z -               '* CAPEC: [CAPEC-105: HTTP Request Splitting](https://capec.mitre.org/data/definitions/105.html)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3089961Z -               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-113](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/113.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3090365Z -               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-79](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3090538Z -             text: '# HTTP Response Splitting\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3091190Z -               'Directly writing user input (for example, an HTTP request parameter) to an HTTP header can lead to an HTTP response-splitting vulnerability.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3091277Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3092900Z +               'Forgery can occur if a user provides some input with characters that are interpreted when the log output is displayed. If the log is displayed as a plain text file, then new line characters can be used by a malicious user to create the appearance of multiple log entries. If the log is displayed as HTML, then arbitrary HTML may be included to spoof log entries.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3094237Z -               'If user-controlled input is used in an HTTP header that allows line break characters, an attacker can inject additional headers or control the response body, leading to vulnerabilities such as XSS or cache poisoning.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3094341Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3094422Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3094548Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3094836Z +               'User input should be suitably sanitized before it is logged.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3095250Z -               'Ensure that user input containing line break characters is not written to an HTTP header.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3095511Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3096757Z +               'If the log entries are plain text then line breaks should be removed from user input, using for example `replace(old, new)` or similar. Care should also be taken that user input is clearly marked in log entries, and that a malicious user cannot cause confusion in other ways.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3096847Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3097557Z +               'For log entries that will be displayed in HTML, user input should be HTML encoded before being logged, to prevent forgery and other forms of HTML injection.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3097652Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3097741Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3097858Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3099776Z +               'In the example, the name provided by the user is recorded using the log output function (`logging.info` or `app.logger.info`, etc.). In these four cases, the name provided by the user is not provided The processing is recorded. If a malicious user provides `Guest%0D%0AUser name: Admin` as a parameter, the log entry will be divided into two lines, the first line is `User name: Guest` code&gt;, the second line is `User name: Admin`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3100646Z -               'In the following example, the case marked BAD writes user input to the header name. In the GOOD case, input is first escaped to not contain any line break characters.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3100734Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3100823Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3100932Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3101089Z +               '#!/usr/bin/env python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3101250Z +               '# -*- coding: UTF-8 -*-\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3101347Z +               '"""\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3101620Z +               '@Desc   ：Log Injection\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3101715Z +               '"""\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3101877Z +               'from flask import Flask\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3102042Z +               'from flask import request\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3102261Z +               'from django.utils.log import request_logger\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3102410Z +               'import logging\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3102579Z -               '@app.route("/example_bad")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3102722Z -               'def example_bad():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3102933Z -               '    rfs_header = request.args["rfs_header"]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3103095Z -               '    response = Response()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3103313Z -               '    custom_header = "X-MyHeader-" + rfs_header\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3103574Z -               '    # BAD: User input is used as part of the header name.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3104062Z -               '    response.headers[custom_header] = "HeaderValue" \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3104235Z -               '    return response\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3104329Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3104545Z +               'logging.basicConfig(level=logging.DEBUG)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3104645Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3104797Z +               'app = Flask(__name__)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3104895Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3105043Z +               "@app.route('/bad1')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3105179Z +               'def bad1():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3105362Z +               "    name = request.args.get('name')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3105589Z +               "    app.logger.info('User name: ' + name) # Bad\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3105725Z +               "    return 'bad1'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3105823Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3105967Z +               "@app.route('/bad2')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3106091Z +               'def bad2():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3106277Z +               "    name = request.args.get('name')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3106493Z +               "    logging.info('User name: ' + name) # Bad\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3106853Z +               "    return 'bad2'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3106957Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3107108Z +               "@app.route('/bad3')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3107239Z +               'def bad3():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3107423Z +               "    name = request.args.get('name')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3107653Z +               "    request_logger.warn('User name: ' + name) # Bad\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3107794Z +               "    return 'bad3'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3107893Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3108032Z +               "@app.route('/bad4')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3108161Z +               'def bad4():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3108344Z +               "    name = request.args.get('name')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3108537Z +               "    logtest = logging.getLogger('test')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3108750Z +               "    logtest.debug('User name: ' + name) # Bad\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3108894Z +               "    return 'bad4'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3108985Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3109144Z +               "if __name__ == '__main__':\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3109427Z +               '    app.debug = True\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3109629Z +               "    handler = logging.FileHandler('log')\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3109818Z +               '    app.logger.addHandler(handler)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3109947Z +               '    app.run()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3110046Z +               '\n' +
