2026-10-20T21:06:14.3110359Z -               'def example_bad():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3110569Z -               '    rfs_header = request.args["rfs_header"]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3110725Z -               '    response = Response()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3111173Z -               '    custom_header = "X-MyHeader-" + rfs_header.replace("\\n", "").replace("\\r","").replace(":","")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3111458Z -               '    # GOOD: Line break characters are removed from the input.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3111702Z -               '    response.headers[custom_header] = "HeaderValue" \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3111852Z -               '    return response\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3111944Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3113004Z +               'In a good example, the program uses the `replace` function to provide parameter processing to the user, and replace `\\r\\n` and `\\n` with empty characters. To a certain extent, the occurrence of log injection vulnerabilities is reduced.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3113093Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3113190Z +               '\n' +
