2026-10-20T21:06:14.3309661Z +               "Commented-out code is distracting and confusing for developers who read the surrounding code, and its significance is often unclear. It will not get compiled or tested when the code around it changes, so it's likely to break over time. For these reasons, commented-out code should be avoided.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3309842Z -             markdown: '# Unused local variable\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3310254Z -               'A local variable is defined (by an assignment) but never used.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3310337Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3311785Z -               'It is sometimes necessary to have a variable which is not used. These unused variables should have distinctive names, to make it clear to readers of the code that they are deliberately not used. The most common conventions for indicating this are to name the variable `_` or to start the name of the variable with `unused` or `_unused`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3311874Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3312251Z -               'The query accepts the following names for variables that are intended to be unused:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3312347Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3312573Z -               '* Any name consisting entirely of underscores.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3312740Z -               '* Any name containing `unused`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3312908Z -               '* The names `dummy` or `empty`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3313117Z -               '* Any "special" name of the form `__xxx__`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3314118Z -               'Variables that are defined in a group, for example `x, y = func()` are handled collectively. If they are all unused, then this is reported. Otherwise they are all treated as used.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3314223Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3314319Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3314443Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3315296Z +               'Remove or reinstate the commented-out code. If you want to include a snippet of example code in a comment, consider enclosing it in quotes or marking it up as appropriate for the source language.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3316379Z -               'If the variable is included for documentation purposes or is otherwise intentionally unused, then change its name to indicate that it is unused, otherwise delete the assignment (taking care not to delete right hand side if it has side effects).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3316465Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3316549Z                 '\n' +
