2026-10-20T21:06:14.3370721Z             fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3371271Z +             text: 'A call to an object which is not a callable will raise a TypeError at runtime.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3371564Z -             text: 'Using a variable before it is initialized causes an exception.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3371648Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3371736Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3371903Z +             markdown: '# Non-callable called\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3372917Z +               'If an object is called, `obj()`, then that object must be a callable or a `TypeError` will be raised. A callable object is any object whose class defines the `__call__` special method. Callable objects include functions, methods, classes.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3373161Z -             markdown: '# Use of an undefined placeholder variable\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3373746Z -               'This place-holder variable may not be defined. If this code is executed and the variable is undefined then a `NameError` will occur.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3374064Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3374468Z +               'The `callable(object)` builtin function determines if an object is callable or not.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3374549Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3375944Z +               'When the Python interpreter attempts to evaluate a call such as `func(arg)` it will invoke the `__call__` special method on `func`. Thus, `func(arg)` is roughly equivalent to `type(func).__call__(func, arg)` which means that the *class* must define the attribute `__call__`, merely adding it to the instance is not sufficient.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3376042Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3376131Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3376256Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3376761Z +               'Since this problem usually indicates a logical error, it is not possible to give a general recipe for fixing it.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3377702Z -               'Check that the name of the place-holder variable is not a typographic error. If the name is correct, either define a value for the variable, or import the module that defines the function or method that sets the value.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3377792Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3378713Z -               'If another module initializes this variable before it is used, then the `NameError` may not occur. However, you can make the code more robust and clearer by setting the variable to a default value in its own module.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3378792Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3378923Z +               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3379418Z +               '`list`s are not callable. In this example, an attempt is made to call a `list` which will fail with a `TypeError`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3379496Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3379750Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3379885Z +               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3380011Z +               'a_list = []\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3380141Z +               'a_list()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3380231Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3380329Z +               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3380422Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3380533Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3380991Z +               '* Python Standard Library: [callable](http://docs.python.org/2/library/functions.html#callable).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3381506Z +               '* Python Language Reference: [object.__call__](http://docs.python.org/2/reference/datamodel.html#object.__call__).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3381666Z +             text: '# Non-callable called\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3382676Z +               'If an object is called, `obj()`, then that object must be a callable or a `TypeError` will be raised. A callable object is any object whose class defines the `__call__` special method. Callable objects include functions, methods, classes.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3383188Z -               '* Python Standard Library: [NameError](https://docs.python.org/library/exceptions.html#exceptions.NameError).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3383541Z -             text: '# Use of an undefined placeholder variable\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3384374Z -               'This place-holder variable may not be defined. If this code is executed and the variable is undefined then a `NameError` will occur.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3384469Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3384843Z +               'The `callable(object)` builtin function determines if an object is callable or not.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3384926Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3386297Z +               'When the Python interpreter attempts to evaluate a call such as `func(arg)` it will invoke the `__call__` special method on `func`. Thus, `func(arg)` is roughly equivalent to `type(func).__call__(func, arg)` which means that the *class* must define the attribute `__call__`, merely adding it to the instance is not sufficient.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3386389Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3386491Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3386617Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3387106Z +               'Since this problem usually indicates a logical error, it is not possible to give a general recipe for fixing it.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3388049Z -               'Check that the name of the place-holder variable is not a typographic error. If the name is correct, either define a value for the variable, or import the module that defines the function or method that sets the value.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3388135Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3389050Z -               'If another module initializes this variable before it is used, then the `NameError` may not occur. However, you can make the code more robust and clearer by setting the variable to a default value in its own module.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3389138Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3389267Z +               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3389747Z +               '`list`s are not callable. In this example, an attempt is made to call a `list` which will fail with a `TypeError`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3389831Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3389926Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3390045Z +               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3390174Z +               'a_list = []\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3390292Z +               'a_list()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3390390Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3390490Z +               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3390579Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3390694Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3391137Z +               '* Python Standard Library: [callable](http://docs.python.org/2/library/functions.html#callable).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3391784Z +               '* Python Language Reference: [object.__call__](http://docs.python.org/2/reference/datamodel.html#object.__call__).\n'
