2026-10-20T21:06:14.3598866Z +             markdown: '# Comparison of identical values\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3599802Z +               "When two identical expressions are compared it is typically an indication of a mistake, since the Boolean value of the comparison will always be the same, unless the value is the floating point value `float('nan')`.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3600159Z -             markdown: '# Variable defined multiple times\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3600738Z -               'Multiple assignments to a single variable without an intervening usage makes the first assignment redundant. Its value is lost.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3600824Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3600910Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3601036Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3602407Z +               'It is not good practice to compare a value with itself, as it makes the code hard to read and can hide errors with classes that do not correctly implement equality. If testing whether a floating-point value is not-a-number, then use `math.isnan()`. If the value may be a complex number, then use `cmath.isnan()` instead.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3603083Z -               'Ensure that the second assignment is in fact correct. Then delete the first assignment (taking care not to delete right hand side if it has side effects).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3603170Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3603252Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3603365Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3604340Z +               "In this example `f == f` is used to check for `float('nan')`. This makes the code difficult to understand as the reader may not be immediately familiar with this pattern.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3605112Z -               'In this example, `x` is assigned the value of 42 but then the value is changed to 12 before `x` is used. This makes the first assignment useless.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3605204Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3605290Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3605401Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3605497Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3605749Z +               "#Using 'x == x' to check that 'x' is not a float('nan').\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3605889Z +               'def is_normal(f):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3606083Z +               '    return not cmath.isinf(f) and f == f\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3606183Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3606384Z +               '#Improved version; intention is explicit.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3606523Z +               'def is_normal(f):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3606760Z +               '    return not cmath.isinf(f) and not cmath.isnan(f)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3606866Z -               'x = 42\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3606968Z -               'x = 12\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3607073Z -               'print x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3607163Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3607250Z                 '\n' +
