2026-10-20T21:06:14.3664445Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3664625Z +             markdown: '# Redundant comparison\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3665768Z +               'The result of certain comparisons can sometimes be inferred from their context and the results of other comparisons. This can be an indication of faulty logic and may result in dead code or infinite loops if, for example, a loop condition never changes its value.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3666051Z -             markdown: "# Module is imported with 'import' and 'import from'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3666443Z -               'Importing a module twice using the `import xxx` and `from xxx import yyy` is confusing.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3666534Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3666615Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3666738Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3667239Z +               'Inspect the code to check whether the logic is correct, and consider simplifying the logical expression.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3667577Z -               'Remove the `from xxx import yyy` statement. Add `yyy = xxx.yyy` if required.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3667663Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3667749Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3667856Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3668637Z +               'In the following (real world) example the test `obj1 < obj2` is repeated and thus the second test will always be false, and the function `_compare` will only ever return `0` or `-1`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3668866Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3668960Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3669072Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3669218Z +               '  class KeySorter:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3669344Z -               'import os\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3669489Z -               'from os import walk\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3669569Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3669737Z +               '      def __init__(self, obj):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3669887Z +               '          self.obj = obj\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3669977Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3670140Z +               '      def __lt__(self, other):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3670376Z +               '          return self._compare(self.obj, other.obj) < 0\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3670465Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3670649Z +               '      def _compare(self, obj1, obj2):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3670803Z +               '          if obj1 < obj2:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3670956Z +               '              return -1\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3671113Z +               '          elif obj1 < obj2:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3671382Z +               '              return 1\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3671519Z +               '          else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3671660Z +               '              return 0\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3671749Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3671836Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3671914Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3672030Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3672515Z +               '* Python Language Reference: [Comparisons](http://docs.python.org/2/reference/expressions.html#not-in).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3672918Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-561](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/561.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3673318Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-570](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/570.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3673711Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-571](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/571.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3674121Z +             text: '# Redundant comparison\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3675297Z +               'The result of certain comparisons can sometimes be inferred from their context and the results of other comparisons. This can be an indication of faulty logic and may result in dead code or infinite loops if, for example, a loop condition never changes its value.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3675819Z -               '* Python Language Reference: [The import statement](http://docs.python.org/2/reference/simple_stmts.html#import).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3676088Z -             text: "# Module is imported with 'import' and 'import from'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3676475Z -               'Importing a module twice using the `import xxx` and `from xxx import yyy` is confusing.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3676561Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3676644Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3676769Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3677239Z +               'Inspect the code to check whether the logic is correct, and consider simplifying the logical expression.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3677576Z -               'Remove the `from xxx import yyy` statement. Add `yyy = xxx.yyy` if required.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3677666Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3677750Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3677857Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3678636Z +               'In the following (real world) example the test `obj1 < obj2` is repeated and thus the second test will always be false, and the function `_compare` will only ever return `0` or `-1`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3678724Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3678813Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3682763Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3683164Z +               '  class KeySorter:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3683315Z -               'import os\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3683476Z -               'from os import walk\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3683563Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3683746Z +               '      def __init__(self, obj):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3684240Z +               '          self.obj = obj\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3684335Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3684507Z +               '      def __lt__(self, other):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3684756Z +               '          return self._compare(self.obj, other.obj) < 0\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3684846Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3685035Z +               '      def _compare(self, obj1, obj2):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3685185Z +               '          if obj1 < obj2:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3685338Z +               '              return -1\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3685495Z +               '          elif obj1 < obj2:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3685640Z +               '              return 1\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3685774Z +               '          else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3685915Z +               '              return 0\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3686168Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3686259Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3686337Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3686456Z                 '## References\n' +
