2026-10-20T21:06:14.3768389Z +               'When two string literals abut each other the Python interpreter implicitly concatenates them into a single string. On occasion this can be useful, but is more commonly misleading or incorrect.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3768579Z -             markdown: '# Module imports itself\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3769269Z -               'There is no need for a module to import itself. A module importing itself may lead to errors as the module may be in an incomplete state when imported by itself.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3769353Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3769439Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3769560Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3770121Z +               'If the concatenation is deliberate, then use `+` to join the strings. This has no runtime overhead, and makes the intention clear.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3770700Z -               'Remove the import statement. Convert all expressions of the form `mod.name` where "mod" is the name of the current module to `name`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3770809Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3770904Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3771015Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3772023Z +               'In the first function below, `unclear`, implicit string concatenation is used twice; once deliberately and once by accident. In the second function, `clarified`, the first concatenation is made explicit and the second is removed.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3772585Z -               'In this example the module, `ModuleImportsItself` imports itself and has an expression referencing the module it is in as well.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3772672Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3772754Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3772858Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3773025Z -               'import ModuleImportsItself\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3773104Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3773238Z +               'def unclear():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3773743Z +               '    # Returns [ "first part of long string and the second part", "/usr/local/usr/bin" ]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3774148Z +               '    return [\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3774307Z -               'def factorial(n):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3774437Z -               '    if n <= 0:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3774567Z -               '        return 1\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3774808Z -               '    return n * ModuleImportsItself.factorial(n - 1)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3774910Z -               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3775229Z -               'The import can be removed and the reference can be corrected.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3775316Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3775493Z +               '        "first part of long string"\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3775663Z +               '        " and the second part",\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3775804Z +               '        "/usr/local"\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3775935Z +               '        "/usr/bin"\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3776041Z +               '    ]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3776125Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3776258Z +               'def clarified():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3776644Z +               '    # Returns [ "first part of long string and the second part", "/usr/local", "/usr/bin" ]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3776923Z +               '    return [\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3777104Z +               '        "first part of long string" +\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3777271Z +               '        " and the second part",\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3777409Z +               '        "/usr/local",\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3777545Z +               '        "/usr/bin"\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3777645Z +               '    ]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3777764Z -               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3777848Z                 '\n' +
