2026-10-20T21:06:14.3799495Z +             markdown: '# Result of integer division may be truncated\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3800043Z +               'In Python 2, the result of dividing two integers is silently truncated into an integer. This may lead to unexpected behavior.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3800251Z -             markdown: '# Import of deprecated module\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3801262Z -               'A module is deprecated when it cannot or will not be maintained indefinitely in the standard library. Deprecated modules may not receive security fixes or other important updates. See PEP 4 for a list of all deprecated modules.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3801346Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3801430Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3801557Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3802548Z +               'If the division should never be truncated, add `from __future__ import division` to the beginning of the file. If the division should always be truncated, replace the division operator `/` with the truncated division operator `//`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3802986Z -               'Do not import the deprecated module. Replace uses of it with uses of a better maintained module.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3803072Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3803150Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3803279Z +               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3805083Z +               'The first example shows a function for calculating the average of a sequence of numbers. When the function runs under Python 2, and the sequence contains only integers, an incorrect result may be returned because the result is truncated. The second example corrects this error by following the recommendation listed above.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3805189Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3805285Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3805411Z +               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3805539Z +               '# Incorrect:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3805633Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3805771Z +               'def average(l):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3805924Z +               '    return sum(l) / len(l)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3806018Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3806214Z +               'print average([1.0, 2.0])  # Prints "1.5".\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3806481Z +               'print average([1, 2])      # Prints "1", which is incorrect.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3806577Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3806671Z +               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3806763Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3806883Z +               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3807004Z +               '# Correct:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3807179Z +               'from __future__ import division\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3807277Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3807407Z +               'def average(l):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3807691Z +               '    return sum(l) / len(l)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3807781Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3807977Z +               'print average([1.0, 2.0])  # Prints "1.5".\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3808170Z +               'print average([1, 2])      # Prints "1.5".\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3808258Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3808355Z +               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3808449Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3808560Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3809241Z +               '* Python Language Reference: [Binary arithmetic operations](https://docs.python.org/2/reference/expressions.html#binary-arithmetic-operations).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3809643Z +               '* PEP 238: [Changing the Division Operator](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0238/).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.3809981Z +               '* PEP 236: [Back to the __future__](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0236/).\n',
