2026-10-20T21:06:14.4025984Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4026203Z +             markdown: '# Formatted object is not a mapping\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4028011Z +               'If a format string includes conversion specifiers of the form `%(name)s` then the right hand side of the operation must be a mapping. A string is a format string if it appears on the left of a modulo (`%`) operator, the right hand side being the value to be formatted. If the right hand side is not a mapping then a `TypeError` will be raised. Mappings are usually `dict`s but can be any type that implements the mapping protocol.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4028183Z -             markdown: '# Encoding error\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4029141Z -               'Encoding errors prevent a module being evaluated and thus imported. An attempt to import a module with an invalid encoding will fail; a `SyntaxError` will be raised. Note that in Python 2, the default encoding is ASCII.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.4029223Z                 '\n' +
